      "statistical_clipping_imputation_winsorization_or_daily_substitution_allowed": false
    },
    "hypothesis": "A high value means repeated positive minute-return continuations dominate repeated negative continuations; order-sensitive demand persistence may survive from the next open through the third close.",
    "economic_distinction": "This factor counts the order of adjacent minute-return signs and ignores return magnitudes. It is not net return, late return, terminal close location, VWAP location, realized volatility, upside semivariance share, afternoon amount-weighted efficiency, drawdown recovery, amount entropy, or amount serial persistence. Permuting the same multiset of returns can change this factor while leaving magnitude-only and sign-composition statistics unchanged.",
